     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Stan,<div><br></div><div>I am translating a matlab code to Stan. The goal is to create a exponential decay matrix and </div><div>apply it to a reward history (either 0 or 1) of some of the subjects, and finally sum them up </div><div>to get the cumulative reward. Assume my discounting parameter gamma = 0.7. For instance, </div><div>in the past 5 trials, I have:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.1681</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.1681</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.1681</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.1681</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\">       </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.2401</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.2401</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.2401</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.2401</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\">       </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.3430</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.3430</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.3430</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.3430</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\">   </span><span style=\"color:#660\">.*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.4900</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.4900</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.4900</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.4900</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\">       </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.7000</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.7000</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.7000</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.7000</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\">       </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div>which leads a new matrix, and what I need is the column sum.</div><div><br></div><div>In matlab, I could do something like:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><div>    if t &lt;= 2</div><div>        cr(t,:) = ones(1,4)*0.25;</div><div>    else</div><div>        wght = repmat(gamma.^(t-1:-1:1)&#39;,1,4);</div><div>        cr(t,:) = sum(wght.*<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">otherReward(1:t-1,:)</span>,1); <span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">        </span></div><div>        cr(t,:) = exp(cr(t,:)) ./ (sum(exp(cr(t,:)))+eps);</div><div>    end</div></div></code></div><br></div><div>However in Stan, (1) as parameter &#39;wght&#39; changes size every trial,  (2) the power expression (^) does not </div><div>support vectorization, (3) there is no such a direct way to calculate the column sum. I coded something as below.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nSubjects</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nTrials</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      <br>      matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> wgtrew</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      <br>      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">if</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        cr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> initCR</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;  // [0.25 0.25 0.25]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">else</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ct </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>          wgtrew</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ct</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">disc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">^</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ct</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> to_row_vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">otherReward</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ct</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">o </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>          cr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">o</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sub_col</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">wgtrew</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">o</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">));</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>        </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}<br></span><span style=\"color:#000\">        cr[t] &lt;- cr[t]/ (sum(cr[t])+machine_precision());<br>      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>     </span><span style=\"color:#660\">......</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      <br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></font></div></code></div><br>All the other part remains identical to another alternative model, which runs fairly fast. I doubt it is this piece computing </div><div>slows down the sampling procedure. </div><div><br></div><div>I was just wondering if there is a way to optimize it (something comparable in matlab)?</div><div><br></div><div>Hop this post is not so off topic. I appreciate any suggestion or comment.</div><div><br></div><div>Lei</div><div> </div></div>"
